1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:05,432
Today, a green side dish for your gut! I'm cooking garlic broccoli!

2
00:00:06,432 --> 00:00:12,975
One hundred fifty grams of broccoli, one garlic clove, one teaspoon of oil, and two tablespoons of water.

3
00:00:13,975 --> 00:00:19,109
Wash and cut into bite-sized florets. Thinly slice the stalk, so you can eat that too!

4
00:00:20,109 --> 00:00:25,774
Put broccoli and water in the pan. Cover and cook over medium heat for about three minutes.

5
00:00:26,774 --> 00:00:34,060
Let the water evaporate, then turn the heat to medium-low. Add oil and minced garlic. Fry for about one minute.

6
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:40,141
Once the stalks are tender, it's ready! Season lightly, just how you like it.

7
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:48,489
Broccoli adds fiber. Fiber and enough fluids help keep stools soft and easier to pass.

8
00:00:49,489 --> 00:00:55,684
Build up your fiber slowly, rather than all at once! And remember water. That's Chef Gut's tip!

9
00:00:56,684 --> 00:01:01,900
Don't just save my vegetables. Save me a glass of water too! I'm thirsty!

10
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:11,900
Subscribe for your employee badge! Likes are your bonus!
